Title:
0xM0nCrush: Cross-version Windows EDR process terminator (BYOVD)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
0xM0nCrush is a Windows 10/11 process-killing utility that uses a signed HONOR kernel driver (MonProcessEX.sys) to terminate target processes from kernel context via a single IOCTL. It aims to reliably kill EDR/AV and other protected processes across Windows builds without relying on kernel offsets, PDB symbols, or build-specific shellcode. The user-mode Rust binary enumerates processes, resolves PIDs for configured target names, opens `\\.\MonProcessEX`, and issues `DeviceIoControl` to trigger kernel-mode termination, including bypassing Protected Process Light (PPL) checks. Operational features include SCM-based driver install/start/cleanup, randomized service name, optional repeat/jitter loops, dry-run, JSON output, and self-destruct. It’s primarily useful for red teams and offensive security researchers evaluating BYOVD-based EDR disruption, and for defenders as a concrete example to build detections around driver load + IOCTL behavior.

Technical Focus:
- BYOVD using a signed third-party kernel driver (MonProcessEX.sys)
- Kernel-mode process termination via device IOCTL (`0x22400C`)
- PPL/protected process termination bypass mechanics
- SCM driver service lifecycle (install/start/stop/delete) and artifact minimization
- Cross-version stability by avoiding offsets/symbol dependencies
- Host-based detection opportunities (driver load, device handle, IOCTL telemetry)

Use Cases:
- Disable/kill EDR and security agent processes during authorized engagements
- Test resilience of endpoint protections against BYOVD-based tampering
- Develop and validate detections for suspicious driver loads and IOCTL patterns
- Automate process disruption workflows via JSON output/exit codes in C2 pipelines
- Research cross-version kernel kill primitives without per-build adaptation

Keywords:
BYOVD, vulnerable driver, signed driver, MonProcessEX.sys, HONOR driver, Windows kernel, IOCTL 0x22400C, DeviceIoControl, CreateFileW, Service Control Manager, SCM, PPL bypass, Protected Process Light, EPROCESS, process termination, EDR killer, Windows 10, Windows 11, Rust, LOLDrivers